/T (Ans: The Ternary operator is the operator that is used to show the conditional statements. This consists of the true or false values with a statement that has to be evaluated for it.  Syntax:  The Ternary operator will be given as:  [on_true] if [expression] else [on_false]x, y = 25, 50big = x if x < y else y  Example: The expression gets evaluated like if x<y else y, in this case if x<y is true then the  value is returned as big=x and if it is incorrect then big=y will be sent as a result. )
/E (Ans: The Ternary operator is the operator that is used to show the conditional statements. This consists of the true or false values with a statement that has to be evaluated for it.  Syntax:  The Ternary operator will be given as:  [on_true] if [expression] else [on_false]x, y = 25, 50big = x if x < y else y  Example: The expression gets evaluated like if x<y else y, in this case if x<y is true then the  value is returned as big=x and if it is incorrect then big=y will be sent as a result. )
