2040 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H5
/T (a\) they are used to indicate a private variables of a class b\) they confuse the interpreter c\) they are used to indicate global variables d\) they slow down execution  Answer: a\) they are used to indicate a private variable of a class  As Python has no concept of private variables, leading underscores are used to  indicate variables that must not be accessed from outside the class. )
/E (a\) they are used to indicate a private variables of a class b\) they confuse the interpreter c\) they are used to indicate global variables d\) they slow down execution  Answer: a\) they are used to indicate a private variable of a class  As Python has no concept of private variables, leading underscores are used to  indicate variables that must not be accessed from outside the class. )
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [18]
>>
